ike kruger did back then  hanji was ecstatically waiting to greet  the malian soldiers and i'll explain why  the scouts were already prepared for  mali to arrive  to put it simply after the events of  last season everyone and parodies became  aware  that the world considered them to be an  enemy they knew that at some point in  the near future  marley would attempt to invade once  again because the island is seen as an  existential threat to humanity as a  result they set up this camp near the  ocean  with armin and aaron serving as the  defense against enemy invaders  when mali finally arrived hanji's goal  was to learn as much as possible about  the outside world  which is information that only foreign  soldiers would know back then armin was  of a similar mindset to hanji  as he saw an opportunity to gather  information as well and later believing  that they could become friends if  everyone got to know each other  yeah that didn't work out too well in  the end anyway hanji greets the malian  soldiers  but next to her is another soldier from  the first survey ship that went missing  two hours earlier  this guy's name was nikolo and yeah they  were kind of threatening him with a  sword behind his back  in an attempt to kind of like get the  other marlin soldiers to cooperate  the idea was that nicola would play  along with hanji's routine but  as you can see even with the threat of  death he still you know he still wasn't  really up for it  nicolo's hatred for aldians is so  ingrained that he literally wanted the  captain to start firing  even though he himself would likely have  been killed in the process  looking at this opening scene it made it  all the more interesting to see later in  the episode when nicolo was mourning for  an eldian but we'll get to that later  as the malian captain prepared to fire  he was surprisingly assassinated on the  spot by elena before she and her  comrades turned their guns on their  fellow malian soldiers  peak revealed in the last episode that  elena was a follower of zeke  and here we find out exactly what that  means within the malian military there  are countless soldiers who are not  actually malians  but rather they are from nations that  marley has conquered both elena and  onyankapon are examples of these  non-malian soldiers and as a result they  have no real loyalty or allegiance to  the country  when the first survey fleet left for  parodies island zeke had already told  elaine  to shoot her commanding officer if  necessary and to tell the leaders on  parodies what he's seeking to gain  however before we get into what zeke  wants there's a couple of things i  should point out during this flashback  number one is that aaron began to show  his first signs of discontent in this  scene  when he points out that parodies need to  do something to protect themselves  while armin seemed optimistic about the  future aaron was concerned that mali's  military could destroy them in a real  battle  and he reiterates that point later in  the episode insisting that parodies need  something to stop other countries from  attacking them the second thing to point  out is that during elena's initial  meeting with hanji and levi  she foreshadows several things that  we've already seen in the final season  for example she mentions how mali can't  currently invade paradise because  they're at war with an alliance of other  nations  the war that she's referring to is  literally what this season began with  but as an audience we only got to see  the end of it  she also introduces them to new  technologies such as the semi-automatic  pistols  which is now standard equipment for  these soldiers on parodies  another thing was when onyankapon tried  to explain the concept of aerial weapons  much to hanji's amazement and many years  later he would be the one trusted to fly  the airship  during the battle in mali moving on now  elena revealed three years ago that  zeke's true goal  is to free the eldium people but he had  two requests that needed to be fulfilled  before he could achieve that  zeke's first request was that he'd be  accepted onto parody's island  and his second request was that he'd be  introduced to the founding titan  aka eren yeager at this point in the  timeline  aaron and zeke are seemingly the only  people who know how to use the full  power of the founding titan  naturally a lot of people had seen aaron  use the founding titan before  but he never actually told anyone how he  was able to do it in this episode he  finally reveals his secret and says he  only concealed the truth to protect  historia  as obviously you know if he told  everyone then it's possible she may have  been turned into a titan like dinah  fritz  with the full power of the founding  titan parodies would be able to activate  the rumbling and defend themselves that  way  but at this point in the story we still  don't know the full details of zeke's  secret plan  in this exact same scene in the manga  zeke said that if his demands were met  he would guarantee the island's safety  provide them with the latest weapons  give them intelligence that would hurt  mali and act as a middleman between  parodies island  and potential friendly nations around  the world it seems like a pretty good  deal to get all of that  just for bringing the guy to the island  and then introducing him to eren  but naturally a lot of people were  against the idea of you know trusting  this guy after he killed  most of the survey corps despite her  reservations hanji did decide that it  was practical to work with the malian  volunteers  and thanks to the help of elena and  onyankapon paradise was able to  neutralize  30 more malian ships over the next three  years  we know this because present day zeke  already revealed that 32 ships in total  had gone missing  just before we continue be sure to smash  the like and sub buttons if you want to  see more attack on titan breakdowns like  this  anyhow onyankapon and a few other  volunteers helped to modernize the  island  by proposing the plans to construct a  port a port would enable parodies to  potentially trade with other nations in  the future  using the same ships that they captured  from mali this scene was kind of funny  because it showed us just how out of the  loop the people and parodies really are  after 100 years of knowing nothing about  the outside world i say this because  sasha asks onyankapon why his skin is  dark  because yeah i mean if you think about  it there have been no black people on  the island that we've been aware of  so it does make sense that she would ask  this question it was a combination of  curiosity and ignorance  but onyankapon smoothly answers by  telling her that whoever created  humanity  thought it would be interesting to have  different kinds of people in the world  as a side note regarding the port itself  we've previously seen that paris island  already does have a small port that was  constructed decades ago  although that must have been on another  part of the island that port was made by  mali specifically so that they could  turn aldians into  titans so it doesn't exactly have the  best history but you know it's still  there  the episode then progressed to an  interesting moment involving nicolo  which partly proves armin's belief that  malia's and eldens can understand each  other  nicola was the captive marlin soldier  that was threatened by levi in the  beginning  and here we find out that he is also a  chef he was forced to prepare a feast of  seafood  which sasha mercilessly tears into even  to the point where she's crying real  tears  until this point the chef had only shown  a hatred for aldians  but once he saw her enjoyment at his  cooking that hatred began to crack just  a little bit  during these times armin really thought  they could change something  as many mallions were able to overcome  their prejudices against aldians  when given sufficient time to do so he  believed that threatening the world with  the rumbling was not something they had  to do  if they could just talk to other nations  once the port was completed however  being the pragmatist that he is  aaron wasn't really buying armin's  optimism as most of the malians who  arrived on the island  still hated the aldean race aaron knew  that the world's perceptions of aldians  is hard to change  because whether they're good people or  not aliens at the end of the day  they're still human beings that can turn  into these man-eating monsters  getting the world to accept that after  nearly 2 000 years of titan domination  was a pretty unrealistic goal on top of  all of that  zeke only had a few years left to live  at this point so  the you know if they were going to bring  him to paris island then that is also on  a time limit  that's why three years later aaron would  eventually grow frustrated  and begin his own plan to infiltrate  marley and get his brother back to the  island  i thought this part was done really well  when aaron was firing at the shooting  range  only for the scene to transition into  sasha getting hit by a bullet  this was meant to symbolize that sasha's  death was eren's fault  which is something that i think we've  pretty much all accepted at this point  present day armin continues to talk to  someone off screen and wonders if there  was a different more peaceful path they  could have taken  the anime then gives us a small preview  of instagram model aaron before moving  over to mikasa at the cemetery  nicolo had arrived to find out if sasha  really died but was being physically  abused by a random aldean  because niccolo is a marlin volunteer  this is quite an ironic thing to happen  considering the way the aliens  themselves are treated across the world  but it's yet another example that  eldians on parodies can sometimes be no  better  than the people who oppress them after  spending the past three years on the  island  nicolo had affection towards sasha and  appreciated her love for his food  unlike the version of himself that hated  aliens in the beginning you can tell  that he was truly devastated by this  loss  sasha's parents then show up as well as  this girl who is the one that sasha  saved from a titan after her village was  destroyed  this was back in season 2 when the  citizens of connie's village were turned  into titans  and sasha's heroics that day are the  only reason this girl is still alive  moving on aaron and zeke were  immediately separated once they arrived  on the island  as they can't yet be trusted to use the  power of the founding titan  on the airship these two were prevented  from making contact as aaron had his  arms restrained  and zeke couldn't really do anything  because his limbs were chopped off by  levi  now that they're back on parodies zeke  was put under levi's supervision  and transported to this massive forest  full of trees we saw before how the draw  titan is the only one that's really able  to take advantage of this environment  and when it comes to the beast titan  there's really not much he can do  there are no rocks around not to mention  that there's a ton of space for the  scouts to maneuver with their odm gear  zeke is being kept here until they  decide what they're gonna do with him  but in the meantime he does seem to show  some concern for gabby and falco  those two had already been locked up in  prison since arriving on the island so  not much to say regarding that  other than that gabby is clearly  organizing her one-person kill list in  her head  the next thing i need to explain relates  to the anti-malian volunteers as it's  been no secret since the beginning that  they were working for zeke the whole  time  with the man himself now arriving on the  island commander pixis decides to have  these guys restrained  so that they can't make an effort to  communicate with him luckily for them  elena doesn't take it too personally  and the titan transformation serum that  you see on the table was stolen by her  from mali  you may be wondering why powdy's island  would even need such a thing  and the simple answer is that they may  need this serum in the future  so that when it's time to eat aaron or  to eat zeke they'll be able to create  pure titans capable of doing so  i'm not saying they're going to eat  aaron or zeke right now but you know  eventually one day  they're gonna need to eat them before  the curse of emir kills them so you know  it's  necessary for the future of the island  in a dimly lit room armin continues to  talk with someone off screen  as he continues speaking the camera pans  to reveal the person he's been talking  to this whole episode was none other  than annie leonhardt  aka the female titan annie is still  encased inside this crystal after four  years  and is seemingly in an unconscious state  it's a good thing she doesn't need to  eat or drink whilst inside this thing  otherwise she would have died a long  time ago at first glance it might appear  strange that armin is taking time to you  know  speak to the unconscious body of someone  who betrayed them all  but there is actually a couple of good  reasons why he would do this  firstly armin succeeded bertolt is the  colossal titan  and whilst he might not be able to see  berto's memories it's possible that  bertott's feelings may be influencing  armin instead  we know that armin's predecessor had a  long-standing crush on annie  so it's possible that you know that  crush is the reason armin is drawn to  talk to her  additionally armin feels guilty for what  the scouts did in mali  and annie is a great person to talk to  this about as she basically did the same  thing just to parodies instead  the episode ends with mikasa still in  the cemetery and she repeats the phrase  that eren once said to her when they  were kids  back then eren saved her life by killing  two human traffickers that were planning  to sell her  but the third kidnapper managed to grab  him by the neck in this moment he told  mikasa to fight  because if they don't fight then they  can't win and if they don't win then  they're gonna die  eren's words help mikasa to activate her  ackman powers  turning her into the super soldier that  she is today in my opinion  the reason mikasa repeats this phrase at  this moment is to reassure herself that  sasha didn't die in vain  and that the fight against mali was  necessary to ensure their survival  at the same time aaron fixes his hair  into a not so stylish man-bun  and tells his reflection to fight almost  like he's trying to psych himself  up for something that's yet to come with  that said that was my breakdown of  episode 9 of attack on titan season 4.  this was a really solid episode and i  kind of appreciated the way they  rearranged certain things when compared  to the manga  to me the flashbacks were a lot less  confusing than they might have been so  yeah they really did a good job in  the pacing and also the organization of  the flashbacks  overall this episode gets an 8 out of  10. as usual i'd appreciate if you  dropped a like on this video  and share it with any attack on titan  fans who you think might not understand  what happened in this episode  thanks for watching as always and until  the next one peace out

