 to grab  him by the neck in this moment he told  mikasa to fight  because if they don't fight then they  can't win and if they don't win then  they're gonna die  eren's words help mikasa to activate her  ackman powers  turning her into the super soldier that  she is today in my opinion  the reason mikasa repeats this phrase at  this moment is to reassure herself that  sasha didn't die in vain  and that the fight against mali was  necessary to ensure their survival  at the same time aaron fixes his hair  into a not so stylish man-bun  and tells his reflection to fight almost  like he's trying to psych himself  up for something that's yet to come with  that said that was my breakdown of  episode 9 of attack on titan season 4.  this was a really solid episode and i  kind of appreciated the way they  rearranged certain things when compared  to the manga  to me the flashbacks were a lot less  confusing than they might have been so  yeah they really did a good job in  the pacing and also the organization of  the flashbacks  overall this episode gets an 8 out of  10. as usual i'd appreciate if you  dropped a like on this video  and share it with any attack on titan  fans who you think might not understand  what happened in this episode  thanks for watching as always and until  the next one peace out
 

